# Converted from the old Grade 2 Survex data (Grade2/Grade2/BackPassage.svx).

# > Ogof Draenen: Back Passage
# 
# Rough compass and tape survey.
# 
# Survey conducted on 15/16 October by Pete Bolt & friends.
# Recording: Phil Thomas
# Tape: Pete Bolt
# Compass:
# Data entry: Tim Long

# Although this lead is off WhiteArch stn 36, the station could not be found, so the survey
# was taken back to stn 34. This looks odd in caverot because it looks like there is
# a crossover. In fact, this is just showing up the width of white arch passage.

# This passage takes it's name from the method of surveying: crawling backwards with the
# tape tied to an ankle! Phil thomas also wrote the survey notes in mirror writing.
# Ironically, he also recorded all the bearings as back-bearings by mistake, so on the
# first attempt, the passage appeared backwards and on the wrong side of White Arch.

survey backpassage

# Station Equivalences

# Data ordering
# In the survey notes, everything was written in mirror-image. I'd like to see
# Survex cope with that! The bearings were all BACK BEARINGS but were recorded as
# normal forward bearings. Thus the From and To columns have been swapped here.

# The survey data

# From   To      Bearing Length  Gradient

centreline
  # BCRA2
  sd length 0.5 metres
  sd compass clino 2.5 degrees
  data normal from to length compass clino
  2	1	7	130	0
  3	2	8	130	0
  4	3	7.5	180	0
  5	4	4.8	155	0
  6	5	10.2	150	0
  7	6	13.6	140	0
  8	7	4.8	160	0
  9	8	6.4	125	0

endcentreline
endsurvey
